'''''Fuchsia arborescens''''', commonly known as the '''tree fuchsia''', is a tree of the genus ''[[Fuchsia]]'' native to Central America. It belongs to the section Schufia and is most closely related to ''[[Fuchsia paniculata]]''.<ref name="Berry2004">{{cite journal |author=Berry, Paul E. |author2=William J. Hahn |author3=Kenneth J. Sytsma |author4=Jocelyn C. Hall |author5=Austin Mast |date=2004|title=Phylogenetic relationships and biogeography of ''Fuchsia'' (Onagraceae) based on noncoding nuclear and chloroplast DNA data|journal=American Journal of Botany|volume=91|issue=4|pages=601–14|doi=10.3732/ajb.91.4.601|pmid=21653416}}</ref>
